.SH NAME
\&ag\-cli\-release\-create \- Create a release
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\&ag\-cli release create [<owner>/<repo>] <tag> [flags]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
\&Create a release for a repository identified by its tag. A non\-empty release body is required by the AtomGit API.
.PP
\&When OWNER/REPO is omitted, the repository is inferred from the current Git repository. An explicit OWNER/REPO argument always takes precedence. Remote selection prefers remote.pushDefault, the current branch upstream, origin, then a unique AtomGit/GitCode remote.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-b, \-\-body <string>\fR
\&Release body text
\&Default: \(dq\(dq.
.TP
\fB\-F, \-\-body\-file <string>\fR
\&Path to file containing release body
\&Default: \(dq\(dq.
.TP
\fB\-n, \-\-name <string>\fR
\&Release name (defaults to tag)
\&Default: \(dq\(dq.
.TP
\fB\-\-prerelease\fR
\&Mark release as a prerelease (release_status=pre)
\&Default: \(dqfalse\(dq.
.TP
\fB\-\-target <string>\fR
\&Target commitish (branch or SHA)
\&Default: \(dq\(dq.
.SH INHERITED OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
\&Show help for command
\&Default: \(dqfalse\(dq.
.TP
\fB\-\-raw\-output\fR
\&Disable terminal output sanitization for machine processing
\&Default: \(dqfalse\(dq.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
\&ag\-cli release create owner/repo v1.0.0 \-\-name \(dqFirst\(dq \-\-body \(dqInitial release\(dq
